    {
        "content": "<p>What Edison said. Here is me slowly writing your <code>apply</code> bit by bit so that we see what's left rather than just timing out.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">homogeneous_radical</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MvPolynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsHomogeneous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">AddMonoidAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsHomogeneous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">AddMonoidAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">radical</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">convert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ideal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsHomogeneous</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">radical</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- works</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  3 goals</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  ⊢ LinearOrder (σ →₀ ℕ)</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  ⊢ IsOrderedCancelAddMonoid (σ →₀ ℕ)</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  ⊢ Ideal.IsHomogeneous (AddMonoidAlgebra.grade k) I</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pick_goal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">convert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- works</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⊢ LinearOrder (σ →₀ ℕ)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- infer_instance fails</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⊢ IsOrderedCancelAddMonoid (σ →₀ ℕ)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- infer_instance fails</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 593862812,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1778267259
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok thank you, this is the issue</p>",
        "id": 593863898,
        "sender_full_name": "Matthew Cotter",
        "timestamp": 1778267629
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>PS an independent issue: rather than <code>open Classical</code> you should probably be writing <code>variable [DecidableEq (σ →₀ ℕ)]</code>, because if in an application <code>\\sigma</code> is a type with decidable equality (e.g. <code>Fin 37</code>) then there's a chance that typeclass inference might be able to find a constructive algorithm for equality on <code>(σ →₀ ℕ)</code> and this will cause problems later on if you have demanded that the algorithm is \"use the axiom of choice\" (which is what <code>open Classical</code> does).</p>\n<p>(PPS this is a textbook example showing how it's best to ask questions on this forum with a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> )</p>",
        "id": 593864476,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1778267790
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, thank you for the advice!</p>",
        "id": 593864953,
        "sender_full_name": "Matthew Cotter",
        "timestamp": 1778267960
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that <code>LinearOrder (σ →₀ ℕ)</code> is not an instance globally</p>",
        "id": 593865034,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778267982
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You probably want <code>LinearOrder (Lex (σ →₀ ℕ))</code></p>",
        "id": 593865103,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778268008
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am assuming this needs a linear order on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">σ</span></span></span></span> (which isn't in the MWE)</p>",
        "id": 593866953,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1778268709
    }
